[2.0.17]
* Update the combined NetBird server to v0.78.2.

[2.0.16]
* Add a dedicated TLS-enabled TCP port for native NetBird management, signal, and relay traffic.
* Keep the dashboard and REST API on Cloudron HTTPS while advertising the selected native client port.
* Document that Cloudron TURN cannot replace NetBird relay authentication and that Reverse Proxy clusters still require public TLS passthrough.

[2.0.15]
* Fix fresh installs falling into unauthenticated login instead of initial owner setup.
* Fix custom STUN ports by using the selected UDP port for both Cloudron exposure and the NetBird listener.
* Verify initial owner creation and setup-state persistence in the runtime smoke test.

